  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/...\n\nThe H5 ridge will continue amplifying over most of the central CONUS \nWednesday and Thursday. The expanding 1000-500mb thicknesses should \nlead to the continued warming trend as most areas see highs in the \nmid to upper 70s those days.\n\nFriday should see one more warm day with highs in the mid 70s. A \npotent H5 longwave trof will progress from the Intermountain West \ntoward the Northern Plains too. Lee cyclogenesis will occur \nwith the sfc low progged to track primarily over the western \nDakotas. However, will likely see a tight pressure gradient \nacross most of OAX. Mixing into a 40 to 45 kt H8 jet may also \nhelp drive down some extra momentum resulting in 40 to 50 mph \ngusts, particularly over far northeast Nebraska. With precip \nchances largely not expected until early Saturday morning, will\nneed to watch that area for fire weather concerns given the dry\nfuels in that area, particularly from cured crops. Some \nportions could flirt with Red Flag Warning criteria, so those \nwith any outdoor plans should keep an eye on the forecast.\n\nPoPs of 40 to 60% return areawide by Saturday morning, tapering off \non Sunday with cooler temps in the mid 60s.",
